<article class="env-lemma" id="02MR">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MR">Lemma <span data-tag="02MR">6.3.6.15</span>.</a> Let $\{  S_{\alpha } \} $ be a diagram of nonsingular simplicial sets. Then the limit $\varprojlim _{\alpha } S_{\alpha }$ is also nonsingular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="02MK" href="/tag/02MK">6.3.6.9</a>, it will suffice to show that the product $S = \prod _{\alpha } S_{\alpha }$ is nonsingular. Let $\sigma : \Delta ^ n \rightarrow S$ be a nondegenerate simplex of $S$; we wish to show that $\sigma $ is a monomorphism of simplicial sets. For each index $\alpha $, Proposition <a data-tag="0014" href="/tag/0014">1.1.3.8</a> guarantees that there exists a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \Delta ^{n} \ar [r]^-{\sigma } \ar [d]^{\tau _{\alpha }} &amp;  S \ar [d] \\ \Delta ^{n_{\alpha }} \ar [r]^-{ \sigma _{\alpha } } &amp;  S_{\alpha }, } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $\sigma _{\alpha }$ is a nondegenerate simplex $S_{\alpha }$. Our assumption that $S_{\alpha }$ is nondegenerate guarantees that $\sigma _{\alpha }$ is a monomorphism of simplicial sets, so that the product map 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \prod _{\alpha } \Delta ^{n_{\alpha }} \xrightarrow { \prod _{\alpha } \sigma _{\alpha } } \prod _{\alpha } S_{\alpha } = S \]
</div>
<p>
       is also a monomorphism. It will therefore suffice to show that $\tau = \{  \tau _{\alpha } \} $ determines a monomorphism of simplicial sets $\Delta ^{n} \rightarrow \prod _{\alpha } \Delta ^{n_{\alpha }}$. Since $\prod _{\alpha } \Delta ^{n_{\alpha }}$ can be identified with the nerve of the partially ordered set $\prod _{\alpha } [n_{\alpha } ]$, it is a nonsingular simplicial set (Example <a data-tag="02MJ" href="/tag/02MJ">6.3.6.8</a>). It will therefore suffice to show that $\tau $ is nondegenerate, which follows immediately from our assumption that $\sigma $ is nondegenerate. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></p></p></article>
